From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 10:55:58 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] lynx-bios

Beetle Lynx has no boot of its own for carts: with no BIOS/lynxboot.img,
or one under 512 bytes, it loads the cart without an error and never
draws. Before a Lynx cart is inserted, from the shelf or resumed at
boot (both go through App::insert), slot reads BIOS/lynxboot.img: a
missing, unreadable, empty or wrong-size file keeps the cart on the
shelf with the refusal shake and the toast "Lynx needs BIOS/lynxboot.img";
512 bytes that are not the known dump (crc32 0x0d973c9d, the core's own
"[BIOS] Atari Lynx" entry) launch with "lynxboot.img is not the known
dump" once a session, since a modified boot ROM may be deliberate. The
toasts are their own list after the disc toasts, so Toast::FIXED and
upstream's toast tests stay as they are. slot never ships or fetches
the file.
